,title,link,text,language,family
0,Sarikoli language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sarikoli_language,"Although to a large extent the Sarikoli lexicon is quite close to those of other Eastern Iranian languages, there are a large number of words unique to Sarikoli and the closely related Shughni that are not found in other Eastern Iranian languages such as Wakhi, Pashto or Avestan.",Sarikoli,Indo-European
1,Sarikoli | PLP,https://www.phoenixlanguageproject.org/sarikoli,"Sarikoli is an Indo-European Pamir language spoken in China and Pakistan. Although Sarikoli is generally referred to as “Tajik,” it is only distantly related to Tajik as spoken in Tajikistan, and contains very different words and grammar.",Sarikoli,Indo-European
